# Swarmarchy foundation packages — the base system, drivers, boot and audio stack.
# Baked into the ISO's offline mirror (install/packaging never installs these
# directly; the base install + drivers do). One package per line; text after '#'
# is a human note — the builder parses only the first token. aarch64 / Snapdragon X.

# ─── Base system ───
base                       # core Arch base meta-package (essential userland)
base-devel                 # compilers/make/etc — needed to build AUR packages
git                        # version control (installer + AUR builds use it)
linux                      # the kernel (ISO builder rewrites this to linux-aarch64)
linux-headers              # kernel headers (rewritten to linux-aarch64-headers; for DKMS)
linux-firmware             # device firmware blobs (Wi-Fi, GPU, etc.)
dkms                       # builds out-of-tree kernel modules (e.g. DisplayLink's evdi)
autoconf-archive           # extra autotools macros — helps some AUR packages compile

# ─── Boot, snapshots & swap ───
#limine                     # the bootloader
#limine-mkinitcpio-hook     # regenerates boot entries when the kernel/initramfs changes
#limine-snapper-sync        # adds Btrfs snapshot entries to the boot menu (roll back a bad update)
#btrfs-progs                # Btrfs filesystem tools
#snapper                    # Btrfs snapshot manager (automatic timeline + rollback)
zram-generator             # compressed swap in RAM (configured by config/zram.sh; used before disk swap)

# ─── Audio foundation (PipeWire stack; the front-ends are in base.packages) ───
pipewire                   # the audio/video server
pipewire-pulse             # PulseAudio compatibility layer
pipewire-alsa              # ALSA compatibility layer
pipewire-jack              # JACK compatibility (pro-audio apps)
gst-plugin-pipewire        # GStreamer ↔ PipeWire bridge (audio in screenshare/recording)
libpulse                   # PulseAudio client libraries (for apps that expect pulse)

# ─── Wayland / GUI foundation ───
qt6-wayland                # Wayland backend for Qt6 apps
gtk4-layer-shell           # lets GTK4 apps draw bars/overlays (layer-shell surfaces)
webp-pixbuf-loader         # render .webp images in GTK apps and thumbnails

# ─── GPU — Qualcomm Adreno X1-85 ───
mesa                       # OpenGL + the "freedreno" driver for Adreno
vulkan-freedreno           # Vulkan ("turnip") driver for the Adreno GPU

# ── AARCH64 / SNAPDRAGON-X TODO (not resolvable from the offline mirror yet) ──
# These are required but live in the AUR or need a Snapdragon-specific source, so
# the ISO's `pacman -Syw` step can't fetch them. Install via an AUR helper (yay) or
# a custom repo — see swarmarchy-iso/BUILD-AARCH64.md. Listed so they aren't lost:
#
#   linux-aarch64 (mainline 6.14+) + qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dtb  # the kernel
#   Qualcomm firmware (ath12k Wi-Fi, Adreno A7xx) — extract from the Windows partition
#   walker            # keyboard-first app launcher (wlroots-native)
#   yay               # AUR helper
#   displaylink       # Plugable DisplayLink adapter driver
#   evdi              # DisplayLink's kernel module (built via dkms, above)
